        {
          "step": "3",
          "title": "SUPPORTS",
          "text": "SUPPORTS\r\nIn order to specify custom support conditions to be checked during aggregation\r\n(e.g., minimum 2 points supported, or just the center point), it is possible to use\r\nthe Support component to define group of points to be supported.\r\nIn order to specify a support direction, a line segment intersecting the Part geometry\r\nis used.",
          "nearby_components": [
            "NumberSlider",
            "NumberSlider",
            "Random",
            "Curve",
            "Jitter",
            "NumberSlider",
            "Brep"
          ],
          "annotation_type": "Scribble",
          "pos": [
            111.2,
            1115.1
          ]
        },
        {
          "step": "4",
          "title": "AGGREGATION BASE",
          "text": "AGGREGATION BASE\r\nIn order to seed the aggregation with a \"base\", the TransformPart\r\ncomponent is used to randomly scatter a number of parts on the \r\nXY plane.",
          "nearby_components": [
            "Curve",
            "NumberSlider",
            "Point",
            "NumberSlider",
            "NumberSlider",
            "Random"
          ],
          "annotation_type": "Scribble",
          "pos": [
            198.5,
            754.1
          ]
        },
        {
          "step": "5",
          "title": "ADVANCED PART",
          "text": "ADVANCED PART\r\nUsing an AdvancedPart, it is possible to also define custom\r\nsupport groups, points which need to be supported at the same\r\ntime to allow the placement of the part.",
          "nearby_components": [
            "Brep",
            "Point",
            "Wasp_Update File",
            "Curve",
            "Wasp_Connection From Direction"
          ],
          "annotation_type": "Scribble",
          "pos": [
            211.2,
            128
          ]
        },
        {
          "step": "6",
          "title": "CONSTRAINTS MODE",
          "text": "CONSTRAINTS MODE\r\nSetting constraints mode to 1 activates\r\nthe check for Local Constraints",
          "nearby_components": [
            "PARTS_NUM",
            "CONSTRAINTS"
          ],
